How can we implement a unique and innovative approach to handle customer complaints in Java?
One approach I have implemented in the past involved using sentiment analysis to categorize customer complaints and route them to the appropriate department for resolution. Here is some example code for this approach:
import com.ibm.watson.developer_cloud.natural_language_understanding.v1.*;
import com.ibm.watson.developer_cloud.natural_language_understanding.v1.model.*;
public class ComplaintHandler {
    public static void handleComplaint(String text) {
        NaturalLanguageUnderstanding service = new NaturalLanguageUnderstanding(
            NaturalLanguageUnderstanding.VERSION_DATE_2017_02_27,
            "{username}",
            "{password}"
        );
        SentimentOptions sentiment = new SentimentOptions.Builder()
            .build();
        Features features = new Features.Builder()
            .sentiment(sentiment)
            .build();
        AnalyzeOptions parameters = new AnalyzeOptions.Builder()
            .text(text)
            .features(features)
            .build();
        AnalysisResults response = service
            .analyze(parameters)
            .execute();
        String category = getCategory(response.getSentiment().getDocument().getScore());
        switch(category) {
            case "positive":
                System.out.println("Thank you for your feedback!");
                break;
            case "neutral":
                System.out.println("We apologize for any inconvenience. A customer service representative will be in touch shortly.");
                break;
            case "negative":
                System.out.println("We're sorry to hear that. Your complaint has been forwarded to our support team for resolution.");
                break;
            default:
                System.out.println("Unable to categorize complaint. Please try again.");
        }
    }
    private static String getCategory(double score) {
        if(score > 0.5) {
            return "positive";
        } else if(score > 0.1) {
            return "neutral";
        } else {
            return "negative";
        }
    }
}
This code uses the IBM Watson Natural Language Understanding API to perform sentiment analysis on the customer's complaint. Depending on the sentiment score, the complaint is categorized as positive, neutral, or negative, and an appropriate response is given. This approach can help to streamline the complaint resolution process and improve customer satisfaction.

