            html += "<h2>\(websites[i])</h2>"
            html += "<p>\(descriptions[i])</p>"
        }
        html += "</body></html>"

        print(html)
    } catch {
        print("Error parsing HTML: \(error)")
    }
}
task.resume()
```
This code fetches the top 10 websites from a website using URLSession, and then parses the HTML using SwiftSoup. It then extracts the website names and descriptions, and stores them in separate arrays. Finally, it generates an HTML page with the website names and descriptions, and prints it to the console. You can modify this code to display the HTML page in a web view or save it to a file.

