How can I optimize my Java code to find the lowest value in an array of integers using a binary search algorithm instead of a linear search method? Here's the current Java code I'm working with:
int[] arr = {5, 3, 7, 1, 9};
int min = arr[0];
for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
   if (arr[i] < min) {
