Yes, it is possible to modify the existing binary search algorithm to handle the situation where the array may contain duplicate values and return the index of the first occurrence of the target value with optimal efficiency. 
Here is the modified binary search algorithm with the additional constraint:
```
function binarySearch(arr, target) {
  let left = 0;
  let right = arr.length - 1;
  while (left <= right) {
    let mid = Math.floor((left + right) / 2);
    if (arr[mid] === target) {
      // Check if the current index is the first occurrence of the target value
      while (arr[mid - 1] === target) {
        mid--;
      }
      return mid;
    } else if (arr[mid] < target) {
      left = mid + 1;
    } else {
      right = mid - 1;
    }
  }
  return -1;
}
```
In the modified algorithm, after finding the target value, we check if the current index is the first occurrence of the target value by iterating backwards until we find the first occurrence. This ensures that we return the index of the first occurrence of the target value with optimal efficiency.

