    public MyClass(IMyDependency myDependency)
    {
        _myDependency = myDependency;
    }
    public void DoStuff()
    {
        _myDependency.DoSomething();
    }
}
```
Finally, when you create an instance of `MyClass`, pass in an instance of `MyDependency` as the parameter. This will inject the dependency into the class. For example:
```csharp
var myDependency = new MyDependency();
var myClass = new MyClass(myDependency);
myClass.DoStuff();
```
This is a simple example of how to implement dependency injection using C# code. There are many frameworks and libraries available that can help you with more complex scenarios.

