To answer your second question, automated machine learning (AutoML) can be used to improve the accuracy of this query and provide insights on the factors that contribute the most to an individual's salary. AutoML platforms can automatically analyze the dataset, identify the most relevant features, and select the best machine learning algorithm to predict the salary based on these features.
Here's some sample SQL code for implementing machine learning algorithms on this dataset using the H2O AutoML platform:
```
-- Load the data into H2O
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_table;
CREATE TABLE h2o_table AS SELECT * FROM table_name;
-- Initialize the H2O cluster
CALL h2o.init();
-- Load the data into H2O
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_table;
CREATE TABLE h2o_table AS SELECT * FROM table_name;
-- Define the predictor and response variables
SET @predictors = 'age, gender, marital_status, degree, years_of_experience';
SET @response = 'salary';
-- Split the data into training and validation sets
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_train;
CREATE TABLE h2o_train AS
SELECT *
FROM h2o_table
WHERE RAND() < 0.8;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_valid;
CREATE TABLE h2o_valid AS
SELECT *
FROM h2o_table
WHERE RAND() >= 0.8;
-- Train the AutoML model
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_model;
CALL h2o.automl('h2o_train', @predictors, @response, 'h2o_valid', 'h2o_model');
-- Get the feature importance
SELECT variable, relative_importance
FROM TABLE(H2O.GET_FEATURE_IMPORTANCE('h2o_model'), 
            CV(FALSE), 
            TABLE_COLUMNS('variable', 'relative_importance')
        );
-- Get the predictions for the validation set
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS h2o_valid_pred;
CREATE TABLE h2o_valid_pred AS
SELECT 
    h2o_valid.*,
    PREDICT(h2o_model, CONCAT('{', @predictors, '}')) AS pred_salary
FROM h2o_valid;
-- Evaluate the model performance
SELECT 
    MSE(h2o_valid_pred.pred_salary, h2o_valid_pred.salary) AS mse,
    R2(h2o_valid_pred.pred_salary, h2o_valid_pred.salary) AS r2
FROM h2o_valid_pred;
```
This code loads the data into the H2O platform, splits it into training and validation sets, trains an AutoML model on the training set, and evaluates its performance on the validation set. It also retrieves the feature importance, which can provide insights on the factors that contribute the most to an individual's salary.
